In article <rabram.56.744963509@unp4861.cc.unp.ac.za> rabram@unp4861.cc.unp.ac.za (Rob Abrams) writes:
>Please could someone explain how to do the following,
> - eat an item (e.g. ring etc...)

Use the e)at command.  Normally you can only eat comestibles (i.e. food).
However, if you are polymorphed into certain monsters types that normally
eat other things, you may be able to eat other items.

> - name a weapon

Use the #name command.  Most of the named weapons cannot be manually named,
though.  They can only be gotten by sacrificing, wishing, occasionally 
getting very lucky and finding one, or other special circumstances.

>Also what is an Elbereth ???
>
Well, the question should be "What is Elbereth."  In Nethack there are two
meanings.  Elbereth is a very ancient and powerful elvish name.  Monsters
respect it.  If you engrave Elbereth on the ground and stand on it, 
monsters will not attack you (although human type monsters and minotaurs
will, and others will still throw things at you and zap you with wands, etc.).

The second meaning is when it is used as in "Hand of Elbereth."  Basically
when you become the Hand of Elbereth you've just gotten tons of intrinsics 
and good karma from you deity, and you're screwed, because now the amount
of time in between successful prayers has gone from something like a 300
turn minimum to something like a 3000 turn minimum.

Hope you've got some food in that case!

